---
import ArticleLayout from '../../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';

// Volumes réels de la gamme PBR — scrape (article PBR)
const gammePbr = [
  ['PBR160', '25'],
  ['PBR220', '79'],
  ['PBR350', '297'],
  ['PBR420', '510'],
  ['PBR500', '925'],
  ['PBR620', '1,758'],
];
---

<ArticleLayout slug="our-pbr-preconditioners">
  <p>
    The first type, well known to manufacturers, allows hydration of around 5
    to 7% water, injected in the form of water and/or steam. The
    temperature can reach 90&nbsp;°C, with a retention time that generally
    does not exceed 30&nbsp;seconds — although this time can be increased with
    a larger volume.
  </p>
  <p>
    Depending on the application, the single-rotor preconditioner is sometimes
    sufficient. However, when mixing and pre-cooking functions are needed, it
    is preferable to work with twin-rotor preconditioners. It is not unusual
    to obtain retention times of 3&nbsp;minutes with moisture levels of around
    25 to 27%. The quality of the mixing owes much to the configuration
    of the paddles on the two shafts: each has its own function, one mixing
    with small paddles, the other holding the product back with paddles of a
    larger surface area.
  </p>
  <p>
    Mixing with water is helped by the injectors, which form a spray; other
    injections are provided for, such as slurries or oil, in order to
    guarantee the evenness of the mix before extrusion.
  </p>

  <h2>The PBR range</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="table-data">
      <caption class="visually-hidden">
        Volumes of the PBR preconditioners in litres
      </caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Type</th>
          <th scope="col">Volume (litres)</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          gammePbr.map(([type, volume]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row" class="model-ref">{type}</th>
              <td>{volume}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</ArticleLayout>
